  "english": [
    "<b>and with her garment open from both sides, and bathing with men,</b> and ignores it.",
    "The Gemara asks: <b>Can it enter your mind</b> that the <i>baraita</i> is referring to a wife who bathes <b>with men?</b> Even a man of the lowest moral character would not allow his wife to act in this manner. <b>Rather,</b> the <i>baraita</i> means that she bathes <b>in a place where men</b> often <b>bathe.</b>",
    "The <i>baraita</i> continues: With regard to <b>this</b> kind of wife, <b>it is a mitzva by Torah law to divorce her, as it is stated: “Because he has found some unseemly</b> matter in her, and he writes her a scroll of severance, and gives it in her hand, <b>and he sends her out of his house…And she goes and becomes another [<i>aḥer</i>] man’s wife”</b> (Deuteronomy 24:1–2). <b>The verse called</b> the second husband <i>aḥer</i>, other, <b>to state that this</b> man <b>is not a peer of the first</b> husband. They are morally distinct, as <b>that</b> first husband <b>evicted a wicked woman from his house and this</b> second man <b>introduced a wicked woman into his house.</b>",
    "If <b>the second</b> man <b>merits, he will send her out, as it is stated</b> in the following verse: <b>“And the latter husband hates</b> her…and he sends her out of his house” (Deuteronomy 24:3). <b>And if not, she will bury him, as it is stated</b> in the same verse: <b>“Or if the latter husband dies.”</b> It is <b>appropriate for him to</b> receive the punishment of <b>death, as that</b> first man <b>evicted a wicked woman from his house and this</b> second husband <b>introduced a wicked woman into his house.</b>",
    "§ The prophet Malachi states in rebuke of those who divorce their wives: <b>“For I hate sending away,</b> says the Lord, the God of Israel” (Malachi 2:16). <b>Rabbi Yehuda says:</b> The verse means that <b>if you hate</b> your wife, <b>send</b> her away. Do not continue living with a woman whom you hate. <b>Rabbi Yoḥanan says:</b> The verse means that <b>one who sends</b> his wife away <b>is hated</b> by God.",
    "<b>And</b> the Gemara explains that <b>they do not disagree. This</b> statement <b>is with regard to a first marriage,</b> i.e., one should tolerate his first wife and not divorce her, and <b>that</b> statement <b>is with regard to a second marriage,</b> in which case the husband should divorce his wife if he hates her.",
    "<b>As Rabbi Elazar says:</b> With regard to <b>anyone who divorces his first wife, even the altar sheds tears over him, as it is stated: “And this further you do: You cover the altar of the Lord with tears, with weeping, and with sighing, insomuch that He does not regard the offering anymore, nor does He receive it with goodwill from your hand. Yet you say: What for? Because the Lord has been witness between you and the wife of your youth, against whom you have dealt treacherously, though she is your companion, and the wife of your covenant”</b> (Malachi 2:13–14). Clearly one should not divorce the wife of his youth, i.e., his first wife, as one who does so is hated by God for divorcing the woman to whom he was bound in companionship and covenant."
  ],
  "gemara": [
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "<span class=\"sentence\" id=\"0\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>וּפְרוּמָה מִשְּׁנֵי צְדָדֶיהָ, וְרוֹחֶצֶת עִם בְּנֵי אָדָם.",
      "segment_ids": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "<span class=\"sentence\" id=\"1\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>״עִם בְּנֵי אָדָם״ סָלְקָא דַּעְתָּךְ?! אֶלָּא בִּמְקוֹם שֶׁבְּנֵי אָדָם",
      "segment_ids": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "רוֹחֲצִין. <span class=\"sentence\" id=\"2\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>זוֹ <span class=\"ein_mishpat_marker\" data-ein-mishpat-id=\"0\" data-marker-letter=\"א\">א</span>– מִצְוָה מִן הַתּוֹרָה לְגָרְשָׁהּ, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר:",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "״כִּי מָצָא בָהּ עֶרְוַת וְגוֹ׳ וְשִׁלְּחָהּ מִבֵּיתוֹ״. ״וְהָלְכָה",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "וְהָיְתָה לְאִישׁ אַחֵר״ – הַכָּתוּב קְרָאוֹ ״אַחֵר״, לוֹמַר:",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "<span class=\"ein_mishpat_marker\" data-ein-mishpat-id=\"1\" data-marker-letter=\"ב\">ב</span>שֶׁאֵין זֶה בֶּן זוּגוֹ לָרִאשׁוֹן – זֶה הוֹצִיא רְשָׁעָה",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "מִבֵּיתוֹ, וְזֶה הִכְנִיס רְשָׁעָה לְתוֹךְ בֵּיתוֹ. <span class=\"sentence\" id=\"3\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>זָכָה שֵׁנִי –",
      "segment_ids": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "שִׁלְּחָהּ, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״וּשְׂנֵאָהּ הָאִישׁ הָאַחֲרוֹן״.",
      "segment_ids": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "וְאִם לָאו – קוֹבַרְתּוֹ, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״אוֹ כִי יָמוּת הָאִישׁ הָאַחֲרוֹן״ –",
      "segment_ids": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "כְּדַאי הוּא בְּמִיתָה; שֶׁזֶּה הוֹצִיא רְשָׁעָה",
      "segment_ids": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "מִבֵּיתוֹ, וְזֶה הִכְנִיס רְשָׁעָה לְתוֹךְ בֵּיתוֹ. <span class=\"sugya-marker sugya-marker-steinsaltz\" data-sugya-kind=\"steinsaltz\" data-sugya-id=\"458\" data-sentence-id=\"4\" data-steinsaltz-label=\"א\"></span> <span class=\"sentence\" id=\"4\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>״כִּי",
      "segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "930px",
      "text": "שָׂנֵא שַׁלַּח״ – <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-tanna\" data-sage-type=\"tanna\" title=\"Rabbi Yehuda bar Rabbi Elai, fifth-generation Tanna\" data-authority-id=\"1395\" data-full-name=\"Rabbi Yehuda bar Rabbi Elai\" data-name-he=\"רבי יהודה ברבי אילעאי\">רַבִּי יְהוּדָה</span> אוֹמֵר: אִם שְׂנֵאתָהּ – שַׁלַּח. <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rabbi Yoḥanan II, second-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"1570\" data-full-name=\"Rabbi Yoḥanan II\" data-name-he=\"רבי יוחנן\">רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן</span> אוֹמֵר: שָׂנאוּי הַמְשַׁלֵּחַ. <span class=\"sentence\" id=\"5\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>וְלָא פְּלִיגִי: <span class=\"ein_mishpat_marker\" data-ein-mishpat-id=\"2\" data-marker-letter=\"ג\">ג</span>הָא בְּזוּג",
      "segment_ids": [
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "930px",
      "text": "רִאשׁוֹן, הָא בְּזוּג שֵׁנִי. <span class=\"sentence\" id=\"6\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>דְּאָמַר <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rabbi Elazar ben Pedat, second-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"467\" data-full-name=\"Rabbi Elazar ben Pedat\" data-name-he=\"רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר בֶּן פְּדָת\" data-resolution-rule=\"amora_context\" data-resolution-explanation=\"Resolved from nearby amoraic interlocutors and discourse.\" data-resolution-reasons=\"[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;heuristic&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Amora context&quot;,&quot;detail&quot;:&quot;Resolved from nearby amoraic interlocutors and discourse.&quot;,&quot;attribution&quot;:&quot;Girsology disambiguation heuristics&quot;}]\">רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר</span><span class=\"ein_mishpat_marker\" data-ein-mishpat-id=\"3\" data-marker-letter=\"ד\">ד</span>: כׇּל הַמְגָרֵשׁ אִשְׁתּוֹ רִאשׁוֹנָה – אֲפִילּוּ מִזְבֵּחַ מוֹרִיד עָלָיו דְּמָעוֹת,",
      "segment_ids": [
        6
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "930px",
      "text": "שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״וְזֹאת שֵׁנִית תַּעֲשׂוּ, כַּסּוֹת דִּמְעָה אֶת מִזְבַּח ה׳, בְּכִי וַאֲנָקָה מֵאֵין עוֹד פְּנוֹת אֶל הַמִּנְחָה, וְלָקַחַת",
      "segment_ids": [
        6
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "930px",
      "text": "רָצוֹן מִיֶּדְכֶם. וַאֲמַרְתֶּם: עַל מָה? עַל כִּי ה׳ הֵעִיד בֵּינְךָ וּבֵין אֵשֶׁת נְעוּרֶיךָ, אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה בָּגַדְתָּה בָּהּ, וְהִיא",
      "segment_ids": [
        6
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "930px",
      "text": "חֲבֶרְתְּךָ וְאֵשֶׁת בְּרִיתֶךָ״<span class=\"sugya-marker sugya-marker-vilna-piska\" data-sugya-kind=\"vilna-piska\" data-sugya-id=\"434\" data-raw-symbol=\"׃\">׃</span>",
      "segment_ids": [
        6
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "930px",
      "text": "<span class=\"sentence\" id=\"7\" type=\"start\">&star;</span><br><br><big><strong>הֲדַרַן עֲלָךְ הַמְגָרֵשׁ וּסְלִיקָא לַהּ מַסֶּכֶת גִּיטִּין</strong></big><br><br>",
      "segment_ids": [
        7
      ]
    }
  ],
  "rashi": [
    {
      "width": "450px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "<b>וּפְרוּמָה מִשְּׁנֵי צְדָדֶיהָ</b> אצל אצילי ידיה כדרך אדומיות שבצרפת",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:1:1",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "450px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "שבשרן נראה מצדיהן: <b>״עִם בְּנֵי אָדָם״ סָלְקָא דַּעְתָּךְ</b> א\"כ רגלים לדבר",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:2:1",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "450px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "שזונה היא ואסורה לו: <b>בִּמְקוֹם שֶׁבְּנֵי אָדָם <span class=\"dh-divergent\">רוחצים</span></b> והיא נכנסת",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:2:2",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "450px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "לעיניהם לאחר יציאתן כשהן לובשין בגדיהן: <b>״כִּי שָׂנֵא שַׁלַּח״</b> פסוק",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:5:1",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "250px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "הוא בנבואת מלאכי: <b>אִם <span class=\"dh-divergent\">שנאת&#x27;</span></b>",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:5:2",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "250px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "<b>שַׁלַּח״</b> כרבי עקיבא: <b>אם</b> <b>שנואה</b>",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:5:3",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "250px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "<b><span class=\"dh-divergent\">היא</span> <span class=\"dh-divergent\">לפני</span> <span class=\"dh-divergent\">המקום</span> שַׁלַּח״.</b> כב\"ש ואית",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:5:3",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "250px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "דגרסי שנוי המשלח וזו שמעתי שנוי",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:5:3",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "250px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "המשלח לפני המקום ואפילו לבית",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:5:3",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "250px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "הלל נהי דלא כייפינן שלא להוציא",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:5:3",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "250px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "מיהו שנוי הוא: <b><span class=\"dh-divergent\">זוג</span> רִאשׁוֹן.</b> אשת",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:6:1",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "250px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "נעורים ובה משתעי קרא כדכתיב",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:6:1",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "250px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "בתריה אשת נעוריך וכתיב",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:6:1",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "250px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "ונשמרתם ברוחכם ובאשת נעוריך",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:6:1",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "250px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": "אל יבגוד:",
      "source_ref": "Rashi on Gittin 90b:6:1",
      "gemara_segment_ids": [
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": "250px",
      "right": "",
      "left": "0px",
      "text": ""
    }
  ],
